---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
const activities=[['Observation of classroom transaction and report writing for ECCE (S1.1)','10'],['Conducting activities with the school students on life skills and prepare a report. (S1.4)','10'],['Organization of Arts creative activities by wall magazine/collage/poster (S1.7) making/clay modeling','10'],['Organization of Yoga (S1.8)','10'],['Preparation of garden in school campus/plantation of medicinal plants/preparation of decorative items by using waste materials for all classes (S1.9)','10']];
const guidelines=['Observe the ECCE classroom transaction in the allotted school and write a report.','Conduct life skill education activities through role play, games and other activities, and prepare a report.','In groups of 3–4, organize at least two Art and Creative Education activities.','Organize a programme on Asanas and Pranayamas, class-wise, for two days in a week.','In groups of 3–4, prepare a flower, vegetable or medicinal garden and organize a programme to prepare decorative items using waste materials.'];
---
<Layout title="School Internship - I"><div class="wrap"><PageHeader title="Your first classroom experience." description="School Internship - I brings your Semester 1 work into the school. Keep the original requirements and your mentor’s guidance close." kicker="SI-I · SCHOOL INTERNSHIP - I" back="/courses/semester-1/" backLabel="Semester 1"/><div class="stats-row"><span><strong>2</strong> weeks</span><span><strong>50</strong> marks</span><span>Included in course internal assessments</span></div><div class="source-note"><strong>Check a source inconsistency with your mentor.</strong><p>The internship table calls the first activity “ECCE (S1.1)”, although ECCE is S1.2 in the course list. The S1.1 paper’s SIP section instead describes child case studies. These differences are preserved here. Your mentor should clarify the expected activity.</p></div><section class="section"><span class="badge">Official table · PDF page 45</span><h2>Activities in the curriculum</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Activity as listed</th><th>Marks</th></tr></thead><tbody>{activities.map(([a,m])=><tr><td>{a}</td><td>{m}</td></tr>)}</tbody><tfoot><tr><th>Total</th><th>50</th></tr></tfoot></table></div></section><section class="section two-col"><div class="content-panel"><h2>Guidelines at a glance</h2><p class="small muted">A summary of the five guidelines on printed page 34; these are not additional institutional requirements.</p><ol class="reading-list">{guidelines.map(g=><li>{g}</li>)}</ol><a class="text-link" href="/curriculum-2024.pdf#page=45">Read the original guidelines ↗</a></div><div class="content-panel"><span class="badge">Student planning aid</span><h2>Keep a simple record.</h2><div class="checklist">{['Confirm the allotted school, dates and tasks.','Plan each assigned activity with your mentor.','Keep observation notes and activity records.','Write your own reflection on the experience.','Check your report against the required format.'].map((s,i)=><label><input type="checkbox" data-check={`internship-${i}`}/><span>{s}</span></label>)}</div><p class="small muted">These reminders help you organize your work. They are not an official assessment checklist.</p><a href="/templates/internship-reflection.txt" download class="button secondary">Download reflection template ↓</a></div></section></div></Layout>
